1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,954
Some content belongs together:

2
00:00:02,954 --> 00:00:05,885
the posts of a blog, the pages of a help center.

3
00:00:05,885 --> 00:00:09,358
The Lists module groups content items in a container item.

4
00:00:09,358 --> 00:00:12,832
You'll see what a list is, how to turn a content type into

5
00:00:12,832 --> 00:00:14,460
one, and how to fill it.

6
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:22,997
A list is a content item that holds other content items.

7
00:00:22,997 --> 00:00:27,061
A blog holds its posts, and a help center holds its pages.

8
00:00:27,061 --> 00:00:33,030
Both the list and its items are ordinary content items, edited in the usual admin pages.

9
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:37,339
A content type becomes a list when it has the List part.

10
00:00:37,339 --> 00:00:40,439
Items created from inside the list belong to it.

11
00:00:40,439 --> 00:00:44,515
Each item remembers the list it was created in, and it belongs to

12
00:00:44,515 --> 00:00:45,950
one list at a time.

13
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:50,547
In the admin, a list gets its own page, with a button to

14
00:00:50,547 --> 00:00:52,346
create items inside it.

15
00:00:52,346 --> 00:00:55,573
On the site, visitors see its published items.

16
00:00:55,573 --> 00:01:00,040
The feature is called Lists, and you enable it in Tools, Features.

17
00:01:04,266 --> 00:01:08,211
A site set up with the Blog recipe has the Lists feature enabled,

18
00:01:08,211 --> 00:01:09,823
and its Blog is a list.

19
00:01:09,823 --> 00:01:12,046
Let's open Blog in the admin menu.

20
00:01:12,505 --> 00:01:14,630
This is the page of the list.

21
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:19,486
Edit Blog changes the list itself, and Create Blog Post adds a post to it.

22
00:01:19,486 --> 00:01:22,035
The posts it holds are listed below.

23
00:01:22,529 --> 00:01:25,018
Each post is a content item of its own.

24
00:01:25,018 --> 00:01:28,945
It remembers the blog it was created in, and this page shows only

25
00:01:28,945 --> 00:01:30,549
the posts of that blog.

26
00:01:34,849 --> 00:01:39,900
To make your own list, start with a content type, which defines a kind of content.

27
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:44,549
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and choose Create new type.

28
00:01:45,441 --> 00:01:46,901
Name it Help Center.

29
00:01:46,901 --> 00:01:50,045
The Technical Name fills in from the Display Name.

30
00:01:50,045 --> 00:01:52,741
Create saves the type and opens Add Parts.

31
00:01:53,553 --> 00:01:55,698
Parts give a type its behavior.

32
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:57,206
Check three of them:

33
00:01:57,206 --> 00:02:01,844
Autoroute gives items a web address, List turns the type into a container,

34
00:02:01,844 --> 00:02:03,873
and Title gives them a title.

35
00:02:04,334 --> 00:02:07,192
Add Selected Parts attaches them and opens the type.

36
00:02:07,192 --> 00:02:09,409
Each part you added has an Edit button.

37
00:02:09,409 --> 00:02:11,724
Let's open the settings of the List part.

38
00:02:12,197 --> 00:02:18,265
The settings are Page Size, Enable Ordering, Contained Content Types, Show container's header,

39
00:02:18,265 --> 00:02:19,843
and Show full pager.

40
00:02:19,843 --> 00:02:22,877
A separate video covers ordering and paging.

41
00:02:23,329 --> 00:02:26,180
A list needs at least one contained type.

42
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:31,276
Contained Content Types lists every content type, so check Page, the type this

43
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:33,339
list holds, and choose Save.

44
00:02:37,554 --> 00:02:39,622
Next, create the list itself.

45
00:02:39,622 --> 00:02:44,526
Under Content, Content Items, the New menu offers Help Center, like any other

46
00:02:44,526 --> 00:02:46,534
content type you can create.

47
00:02:47,148 --> 00:02:49,035
Enter the title Help Center.

48
00:02:49,035 --> 00:02:51,309
The permalink is generated for you.

49
00:02:51,309 --> 00:02:52,474
Choose Publish:

50
00:02:52,474 --> 00:02:55,858
the list is published, and you return to Content Items.

51
00:02:56,324 --> 00:03:00,488
The Help Center row has a button for its items, List Page Items.

52
00:03:00,488 --> 00:03:03,404
It opens the page of the list in the admin.

53
00:03:03,879 --> 00:03:06,841
The page of the list says that it is empty.

54
00:03:06,841 --> 00:03:12,159
Create Page adds the first item, and the editor opens with links back to the list.

55
00:03:12,622 --> 00:03:16,174
Enter the title Reset your password and choose Publish.

56
00:03:16,174 --> 00:03:19,202
You return to the list, and the item is in it.

57
00:03:19,653 --> 00:03:22,464
Save Draft keeps an item unpublished.

58
00:03:22,464 --> 00:03:26,974
Create a second item, Export your data, and save it as a draft.

59
00:03:26,974 --> 00:03:28,673
The list shows both.

60
00:03:29,139 --> 00:03:33,772
Create a third item, Change your email address, and choose Publish.

61
00:03:33,772 --> 00:03:37,199
The list shows all three, the most recent first.

62
00:03:41,411 --> 00:03:46,470
The page of a list shows its items, the most recent first, drafts included.

63
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:50,841
Each row has an Edit button, and published items also have View.

64
00:03:51,312 --> 00:03:55,811
The filter menu next to the search box offers Only draft items, Only

65
00:03:55,811 --> 00:04:00,066
published items, and Owned by me, which keeps the items you own.

66
00:04:00,066 --> 00:04:04,322
Choose Only draft items to see the items that are not published.

67
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:08,843
Open the filter menu again and choose Only published items.

68
00:04:08,843 --> 00:04:12,720
The draft is hidden, and the two published items remain.

69
00:04:13,178 --> 00:04:16,101
The search box filters the items by title.

70
00:04:16,101 --> 00:04:19,998
Search for password, and only Reset your password remains.

71
00:04:24,201 --> 00:04:28,831
In Content Items, View on the Help Center row opens the list on the site.

72
00:04:29,286 --> 00:04:33,267
Visitors see the published items as links, the most recent first.

73
00:04:33,267 --> 00:04:36,126
The draft is not there until it is published.

74
00:04:36,585 --> 00:04:40,140
Selecting a title opens the item on a page of its own.

75
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:44,405
Each item of the list has its own address, like any other content.

76
00:04:46,405 --> 00:04:49,079
A list is a content item that holds others:

77
00:04:49,079 --> 00:04:52,788
add the List part to a type, choose the types it contains, and

78
00:04:52,788 --> 00:04:55,407
create its items from the list's own page.

79
00:04:55,407 --> 00:04:56,825
Thanks for watching.

